## 1. Android Splash Screen Stuck — Root Cause

The crash is **not** the `try/catch` failing silently. The real problem is this sequence in `RootLayout`:

```ts
// Line 176-182
useEffect(() => {
  if (!fontsLoaded) {
    SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync().catch(() => {});
  }
}, [fontsLoaded]);

if (!fontsLoaded) return null;
```

**The bug:** `SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync()` must be called **before** the first render, not inside a `useEffect`. By the time the `useEffect` fires, the splash screen may have already auto-hidden or the call is too late. More critically — `SplashScreen.hideAsync()` is only called inside `NavigationGuard` (line 45), but `NavigationGuard` is a child of `RootLayoutInner`, which is only rendered after `fontsLoaded` is true. If fonts fail to load or are slow, `NavigationGuard` never mounts, `hideAsync()` is never called, and the splash screen stays forever.

**The proper fix — two parts:**

**Part A:** Call `SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync()` at module level (outside any component), before any render happens:
```ts
// At the top of _layout.tsx, outside all components:
SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync().catch(() => {});
```

**Part B:** Add a fallback `hideAsync()` call in `RootLayout` itself (not just in `NavigationGuard`) so if fonts load but routing hasn't fired yet, the splash doesn't hang:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (fontsLoaded) {
    // NavigationGuard will call hideAsync when routing is ready,
    // but set a 3s safety net in case it doesn't
    const timer = setTimeout(() => SplashScreen.hideAsync().catch(() => {}), 3000);
    return () => clearTimeout(timer);
  }
}, [fontsLoaded]);
```

The `expo-navigation-bar` try/catch is fine and not the cause of the hang.

