## 2. `update-shift-status/index.ts` — What happens to `payment_status` when status is set to `cancelled`

**Nothing.** There is no `payment_status` field touched anywhere in this function. The full `updates` object built for a cancellation is:

```ts
const updates: Record<string, unknown> = { status, updated_at: now };
if (status === 'active') updates.started_at = now;
if (status === 'paused') updates.paused_at = now;
if (status === 'completed') updates.ended_at = now;
if (status === 'cancelled') {
  updates.ended_at = now;
  if (cancelled_by) {
    updates.cancelled_by = cancelled_by;
  } else {
    updates.cancelled_by = user.id === session.doctor_id ? 'doctor' : 'requester';
  }
}
if (cancellation_reason) updates.cancellation_reason = cancellation_reason;
```

When `status === 'cancelled'`, the update sets: `status`, `updated_at`, `ended_at`, and `cancelled_by`. **`payment_status` is never set, cleared, or modified.**

