## Answers to your specific questions

### 1. Fields included in the `NEW_REQUEST` broadcast payload to `dispatch:lagos`

The inner `payload` object sent with event `NEW_REQUEST` contains exactly these fields:

| Field | Source |
|---|---|
| `id` | `request.id` |
| `requester_id` | `request.requester_id` |
| `hospital_name` | `request.hospital_name` |
| `hospital_address` | `request.hospital_address` |
| `shift_type` | `request.shift_type` |
| `shift_date` | `request.shift_date` |
| `start_time` | `request.start_time` |
| `end_time` | `request.end_time` |
| `duration_hours` | `request.duration_hours` |
| `coverage_length` | `request.coverage_length` |
| `environment` | `request.environment` |
| `note` | `request.notes` |
| `price` | `request.price` |
| `expiry_at` | `request.expiry_at` |

### 2. Are `requester_rating` and `requester_reliability` included?

**No.** Neither `requester_rating` nor `requester_reliability` appear anywhere in the broadcast payload. They are not fetched from the database, not passed into `broadcastNewRequest()`, and not included in the `NEW_REQUEST` event. The doctor-facing card shown in your screenshot (which displays the star rating and reliability dot indicators) would need these fields added to the broadcast payload to render them from realtime data.

